      "writtenOn": "2021-04-13T18:40:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I probably wasn\u0027t clear. I think this shouldn\u0027t be submitted. I may be misinterpreting the CL, but it sounds like whenever the TYPEC_STATUS command is called, the SOP_*_DISC_DONE events will be cleared. That is not what we want. That means that the AP will never see those bits set, and so a partner and cable will never be registered (so userspace and kernel don\u0027t know that a partner or cable were ever attached).\n\nThe reading or clearing of the bits is not dependent on CONFIG_USB_PD_REQUIRE_AP_MODE_ENTRY  (I\u0027ve explained this a little more in the bug page).\n\nIn any case, it doesn\u0027t solve the issue that the partner is seeing (they still see the MCE error)",
      "parentUuid": "2d8fcd52_f2ebb75a",
